{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.668,
            0.065,
            0.834,
            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Perimeter and Area"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.121,
            0.398,
            0.142
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Perimeter of a triangle"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.146,
            0.622,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": "Consider a triangle having three given sides of lengths 4 cm, 5 cm and 7 cm. Find its perimeter. Perimeter of the triangl $\\begin{aligned} e  &= 4   cm  + 5   cm  + 7 \\\\&= 16   cm .\\end{aligned}$ cm"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.627,
            0.146,
            0.833,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.24,
            0.761,
            0.262
          ],
          "content": "Perimeter of a triangle = sum of the lengths of its three sides."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.279,
            0.59,
            0.344
          ],
          "content": "**Example:** Akshi wants to put lace all around a rectangular tablecloth that is 3 m long and 2 m wide. Find the length of the lace required."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.36,
            0.209,
            0.38
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Solution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.391,
            0.592,
            0.482
          ],
          "content": "Length of the rectangular table cover = 3 m. Breadth of the rectangular table cover = 2 m. Akshi wants to put lace all around the tablecloth."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.613,
            0.283,
            0.854,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_2_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.488,
            0.833,
            0.53
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the length of the lace required will be the perimeter of the rectangular tablecloth."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.535,
            0.833,
            0.606
          ],
          "content": "Now, the perimeter of the rectangular tablecloth = 2 × (length + breadth) = 2 × (3 m + 2 m) = 2 × 5 m = 10 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.611,
            0.608,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": "Hence, the length of the lace required is 10 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.65,
            0.835,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": "**Example:** Find the distance travelled by Usha if she takes three rounds of"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.672,
            0.385,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": "a square park of side 75 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.71,
            0.208,
            0.729
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Solution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.74,
            0.561,
            0.781
          ],
          "content": "Perimeter of the square park = 4 × length of a side = 4 × 75 m = 300 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.787,
            0.479,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": "Distance covered by Usha in one round = 300 m."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.832,
            0.563,
            0.875
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the total distance travelled by Usha in three rounds $3 \\times 300    m  = 900    m$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.578,
            0.678,
            0.88,
